
# Retail Customer Sales – Exploratory Data Analysis

## Project Overview
This project focuses on analyzing retail customer sales data using Python. It explores sales performance, customer behavior, product categories, regional sales and profitability through data cleaning and visualization.

## Objectives
- Clean and preprocess the retail dataset.
- Analyze sales and profit patterns.
- Compare sales across different regions.
- Study product category performance.
- Create visualizations to understand business insights.

## Tools and Technologies
- Python
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Seaborn
- Jupyter Notebook

## Project Structure
- CODE/DATASET – Original and cleaned datasets
- CODE/NOTEBOOK – Python analysis notebook
- CODE/VISUALIZATION – Generated charts
- SYNOPSIS – Project synopsis
- A.V.S. – Project-related documentation

## How to Run
1. Clone or download this repository.
2. Install the required Python libraries.
3. Open the Jupyter Notebook inside CODE/NOTEBOOK.
4. Run all cells to perform the analysis.

